window.__finlexFtShardLoaded("intl_audit_0",[[10009,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Defines and describes the elements and objectives of an assurance engagement (reasonable and limited assurance) and identifies engagements to which ISAs, ISREs, ISAEs, and ISSAs apply."],[10009,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10010,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Requires firms to design, implement, and operate a risk-based system of quality management (SOQM) covering governance, ethics, acceptance/continuance, engagement performance, resources, information/communication, and monitoring/remediation."],[10010,"ISQM 1.19–56","Eight Components of Firm Quality Management (SOQM)","Requires firms to design and operate a proactive, risk-based System of Quality Management (SOQM) covering 8 integrated components: • (1) Firm's risk assessment process (quality objectives → quality risks → responses); (2) Governance and leadership; (3) Relevant ethical requirements; (4) Acceptance and continuance of client relationships; (5) Engagement performance; (6) Resources (human, technological, intellectual); (7) Information and communication; (8) Monitoring and remediation process. • Annual evaluation (ISQM 1.53–55): leadership must evaluate at least annually whether the SOQM provides reasonable assurance that its objectives are being achieved (converged with China QMS 5101)."],[10010,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10011,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the appointment and eligibility of the engagement quality reviewer (EQR) and the reviewer's responsibilities relating to the performance and documentation of an engagement quality review."],[10011,"ISQM 2.17–27","Engagement Quality Reviewer Eligibility, Cooling-Off & Review","• Eligibility (ISQM 2.18–20): reviewer must have competence, capabilities, authority, and objectivity; requires a mandatory 2-year cooling-off period before a former engagement partner can serve as EQR for the same entity (ISQM 2.19(b)). • Performance & timing (ISQM 2.24–26): review significant judgements and conclusions at appropriate points throughout the engagement; engagement report CANNOT be dated before the EQR notifies completion (converged with China QMS 5102)."],[10011,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10012,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Establishes the independent auditor's overall responsibilities when conducting an audit of financial statements in accordance with ISAs, including ethical requirements, professional skepticism, and professional judgment."],[10012,"ISA 200.11–24","Overall Objectives, Audit Risk Model & Professional Skepticism","• Overall objective (ISA 200.11): obtain reasonable assurance about whether the financial statements as a whole are free from material misstatement (whether due to fraud or error) and report in accordance with ISAs. • Core pillars (ISA 200.14–17): comply with IESBA ethical/independence requirements; plan and perform with professional skepticism; exercise professional judgment; obtain sufficient appropriate audit evidence to reduce audit risk (AR = IR × CR × DR) to an acceptably low level (converged with China CSA 1101)."],[10012,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10013,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities in agreeing the terms of the audit engagement with management and, where appropriate, those charged with governance, including preconditions for an audit."],[10013,"ISA 210.6–17","Preconditions for an Audit & Engagement Letter","Establish whether the financial reporting framework is acceptable and obtain management's agreement on its responsibilities (FS preparation, internal control, unrestricted access to information) in a written engagement letter (ISA 210.6, 10)."],[10013,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10014,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the specific responsibilities of the auditor regarding quality management at the engagement level for an audit of financial statements, and the related responsibilities of the engagement partner."],[10014,"ISA 220.13–41","Engagement-Level Quality Management","Engagement partner takes overall responsibility for managing and achieving audit quality, including ethical/independence compliance, sufficient appropriate resources, direction/supervision/review, consultation on difficult matters, and stand-back before dating the report."],[10014,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10015,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to prepare audit documentation for an audit of financial statements sufficient to enable an experienced auditor to understand the nature, timing, extent, and results of audit procedures."],[10015,"ISA 230.7–16","Audit Documentation & 60-Day Assembly Rule","Prepare timely documentation sufficient for an experienced auditor with no prior connection to understand procedures, evidence, and significant judgements (ISA 230.8). Assemble the final audit file on a timely basis — ordinarily not more than 60 days after the auditor's report date (ISA 230.A21)."],[10015,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10016,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities relating to fraud in an audit of financial statements, including reinforced professional skepticism, fraud risk identification, and transparent communication (Revised July 2025)."],[10016,"ISA 240 (Rev. 2025)","Fraud Responsibilities, Presumed Risks & 2025 Revision Highlights","• Fraud triangle & skepticism (ISA 240.12–16): maintain heightened professional skepticism throughout; hold mandatory engagement team discussion on fraud susceptibility. • Two presumed fraud risks (ISA 240.27, 32): (1) improper revenue recognition (rebuttable, must document if rebutted); (2) management override of controls (NEVER rebuttable — mandatory journal entry testing, retrospective review of estimates, and evaluation of significant unusual transactions). • July 2025 Revised Edition highlights: clarifies auditor's role on fraud, reinforces fraud-lens risk assessment aligned with ISA 315, strengthens responses when fraud or suspected fraud is identified, and enhances transparency in auditor's reports (converged with China CSA 1141)."],[10016,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10017,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to consider laws and regulations in an audit of financial statements, including non-compliance with laws and regulations (NOCLAR)."],[10017,"ISA 250.13–29","Consideration of Laws & Regulations (Direct vs. Indirect Effect)","Distinguish laws with direct effect on material financial statement amounts (e.g., tax/pension laws — obtain sufficient appropriate evidence) from other laws where non-compliance could result in material fines/cessation (perform specified inquiry and inspection procedures; report NOCLAR to TCWG/regulators)."],[10017,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10018,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to communicate with those charged with governance in an audit of financial statements regarding planned scope, timing, and significant audit findings."],[10018,"ISA 260.11–22","Two-Way Communication with Those Charged with Governance","Communicate auditor responsibilities, planned scope and timing (including significant risks), significant findings (accounting policies, estimates, difficulties, uncorrected misstatements), and independence statement for listed entities (ISA 260.14–17)."],[10018,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10019,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to communicate appropriately to those charged with governance and management deficiencies in internal control identified in an audit."],[10019,"ISA 265.7–11","Communicating Internal Control Deficiencies","Determine whether identified deficiencies individually or in combination constitute Significant Deficiencies; communicate Significant Deficiencies in writing on a timely basis to TCWG and management (ISA 265.9–10)."],[10019,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10020,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to plan an audit of financial statements, including establishing an overall audit strategy and developing an audit plan."],[10020,"ISA 300.7–12","Overall Audit Strategy & Detailed Audit Plan","Establish an overall audit strategy setting scope, timing, and direction (resources, materiality, key risk areas) and develop a detailed audit plan specifying nature, timing, and extent of risk assessment and further audit procedures."],[10020,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10021,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to identify and assess the risks of material misstatement in the financial statements through understanding the entity, its environment, and its system of internal control."],[10021,"ISA 315.19–38","Spectrum of Inherent Risk, Significant Risks & ITGCs","• Risk identification & assessment (ISA 315.19–34): separately assess Inherent Risk (using 5 inherent risk factors: complexity, subjectivity, change, uncertainty, susceptibility to bias/fraud) and Control Risk. • Significant risk (ISA 315.12(l), 32): an identified risk of material misstatement where inherent risk sits close to the upper end of the spectrum of inherent risk (triggers mandatory substantive responses under ISA 330). • IT environment & ITGCs (ISA 315.26, Appendix 5): identify risks arising from use of IT and evaluate design & implementation of General IT Controls (ITGCs) addressing those risks (converged with China CSA 1211)."],[10021,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10022,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to apply the concept of materiality in planning and performing an audit of financial statements, including performance materiality."],[10022,"ISA 320.10–14","Overall Materiality, Performance Materiality & Revisions","• Overall materiality (ISA 320.10): determined for the financial statements as a whole using an appropriate benchmark (e.g., profit before tax, revenue, total assets). • Performance materiality (ISA 320.9, 11): set BELOW overall materiality to reduce to an appropriately low level the probability that aggregate uncorrected and undetected misstatements exceed overall materiality. • Revise materiality (ISA 320.12) if new information during the audit would have caused a different initial amount (converged with China CSA 1221)."],[10022,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10023,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to design and implement responses to the risks of material misstatement identified and assessed in accordance with ISA 315."],[10023,"ISA 330.5–28","Responses to Assessed Risks: Tests of Controls vs. Substantive Procedures","• Overall responses (ISA 330.5): address financial-statement-level risks (e.g., assign more experienced staff, incorporate unpredictability). • Tests of controls (ISA 330.8–17): mandatory when auditor intends to rely on operating effectiveness of controls OR when substantive procedures alone cannot provide sufficient appropriate evidence. • Substantive procedures (ISA 330.18–23): mandatory for each material class of transactions, account balance, and disclosure; for Significant Risks, MUST perform substantive procedures specifically responsive to that risk (including tests of details if relying solely on substantive procedures, converged with China CSA 1231)."],[10023,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10024,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the user auditor's responsibility to obtain sufficient appropriate audit evidence when a user entity uses the services of one or more service organizations."],[10024,"ISA 402.9–22","Auditing Entities Using Service Organizations","Understand services provided by the service organization; obtain Type 1 (design) or Type 2 (design + operating effectiveness) assurance report under ISAE 3402, or perform direct procedures at the service organization when relying on its controls."],[10024,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10025,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to evaluate the effect of identified misstatements on the audit and of uncorrected misstatements, if any, on the financial statements."],[10025,"ISA 450.5–15","Accumulation & Evaluation of Misstatements","Accumulate all misstatements other than those clearly trivial (ISA 450.5), request management to correct all misstatements, evaluate whether uncorrected misstatements are material individually or in aggregate (including qualitative factors), and obtain written representation on uncorrected items."],[10025,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10026,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Explains what constitutes audit evidence in an audit of financial statements and deals with the auditor's responsibility to design and perform audit procedures to obtain sufficient appropriate audit evidence."],[10026,"ISA 500.6–11","Sufficient Appropriate Audit Evidence & Reliability Hierarchy","• Sufficiency (quantity) and Appropriateness (quality = relevance + reliability) (ISA 500.6, A4–A5). • Reliability principles (ISA 500.A31): independent external sources > internal records; effective controls increase internal reliability; direct auditor-obtained evidence > indirect; documentary > oral; originals > photocopies. • Management's expert (ISA 500.8): evaluate competence, capabilities, and objectivity of any management's expert whose work is used as audit evidence (converged with China CSA 1301)."],[10026,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10027,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with specific considerations by the auditor in obtaining sufficient appropriate audit evidence with respect to inventory, litigation and claims, and segment information."],[10027,"ISA 501.4–13","Specific Evidence: Inventory, Litigation & Segments","Mandatory physical inventory counting attendance if inventory is material (unless impracticable, perform alternative procedures, ISA 501.4–8); inquiry of management/external legal counsel for litigation and claims (ISA 501.9–12); evaluate segment disclosures (ISA 501.13)."],[10027,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10028,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's use of external confirmation procedures to obtain audit evidence in accordance with ISA 330 and ISA 500."],[10028,"ISA 505.7–16","External Confirmations (Positive vs. Negative)","Maintain full auditor control over selection, dispatch, and receipt of confirmations (ISA 505.7). Investigate all exceptions and non-responses via alternative procedures; negative confirmations provide less persuasive evidence and are rarely sufficient alone (ISA 505.15)."],[10028,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10029,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities relating to opening balances in an initial audit engagement."],[10029,"ISA 510.6–13","Initial Audit Engagements — Opening Balances","Obtain sufficient appropriate evidence whether opening balances contain misstatements materially affecting current period and whether accounting policies are consistently applied (review predecessor auditor's workpapers or perform current-period/specific procedures)."],[10029,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10030,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's use of analytical procedures as substantive procedures and near the end of the audit to assist in forming an overall conclusion."],[10030,"ISA 520.5–7","Substantive Analytical Procedures & Overall Review","Design substantive analytical procedures by evaluating data reliability, developing a sufficiently precise expectation, and investigating differences exceeding threshold (ISA 520.5); mandatory analytical procedures near the end of the audit to corroborate overall conclusions (ISA 520.6)."],[10030,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10031,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Applies when the auditor has decided to use audit sampling in performing audit procedures, covering statistical and non-statistical sampling design, selection, and evaluation."],[10031,"ISA 530.6–15","Audit Sampling Design, Projection & Evaluation","Select sample items so each sampling unit has a chance of selection (statistical or non-statistical); project monetary misstatements found in substantive samples to the entire population (ISA 530.14) and evaluate sampling risk."],[10031,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10032,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities relating to accounting estimates and related disclosures in an audit of financial statements, emphasizing estimation uncertainty and inherent risk factors."],[10032,"ISA 540.13–36","Auditing Accounting Estimates: Three Testing Approaches & Bias","• Separate inherent and control risk assessment considering estimation uncertainty, complexity, and subjectivity (ISA 540.16). • Three testing approaches (ISA 540.18): (a) obtain evidence from events occurring up to auditor's report date; (b) test how management made the estimate (method, significant assumptions, data); (c) develop an auditor's point estimate or range. • Stand-back evaluation (ISA 540.33–36): evaluate indicators of possible management bias and reasonableness of disclosures (converged with China CSA 1321)."],[10032,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10033,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities relating to related party relationships and transactions in an audit of financial statements."],[10033,"ISA 550.11–28","Related Party Relationships & Transactions","Remain alert for undisclosed related parties throughout the audit; treat significant related party transactions outside the normal course of business as Significant Risks (ISA 550.18), inspecting underlying contracts for business rationale and fraud indicators."],[10033,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10034,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities relating to subsequent events in an audit of financial statements, covering events up to and after the auditor's report date."],[10034,"ISA 560.6–17","Subsequent Events (Three Time Periods)","Active duty to obtain evidence for events between period-end and auditor's report date (ISA 560.6–9); no obligation to perform procedures after report date, but if material facts become known before or after FS issuance, discuss amendment/reissuance with management (ISA 560.10–17)."],[10034,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10035,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities in the audit of financial statements relating to going concern and the implications for the auditor's report (Revised 2024, published April 2025)."],[10035,"ISA 570 (Rev. 2024)","Going Concern Assessment, 12-Month Window & Reporting","• Management's assessment (ISA 570 Revised 2024, published April 2025): strengthens auditor evaluation of management's going concern assessment over at least 12 months from the date of approval of the financial statements. • Reporting outcomes: adequate disclosure of Material Uncertainty → unmodified opinion with dedicated 'Material Uncertainty Related to Going Concern' section; inadequate disclosure → Qualified or Adverse opinion; inappropriate going concern basis → Adverse opinion (converged with China CSA 1324)."],[10035,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10036,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to obtain written representations from management and, where appropriate, those charged with governance."],[10036,"ISA 580.9–20","Written Representations from Management","Obtain written representations confirming fulfilment of management's responsibilities for FS preparation and completeness of information provided (dated as near as practicable to, but not after, the auditor's report date, ISA 580.14). Refusal triggers Disclaimer of Opinion (ISA 580.20)."],[10036,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10037,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with special considerations that apply to a group audit, including a risk-based approach to scoping components and directing, supervising, and reviewing component auditors."],[10037,"ISA 600.16–59","Risk-Based Group Audits & Component Auditors","• Removes the legacy 'significant component' full-scope bright line in favour of a risk-based scoping approach aligned with ISA 315. • Group engagement partner retains sole responsibility for direction, supervision, and review of component auditors, determining component performance materiality (lower than group materiality), and evaluating sufficiency of group audit evidence (converged with China CSA 1401)."],[10037,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10038,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the external auditor's responsibilities if using the work of internal auditors, including obtaining audit evidence and direct assistance."],[10038,"ISA 610.15–35","Using the Work of Internal Auditors","Evaluate internal audit objectivity, competence, and systematic/disciplined approach before using its work; external auditor remains solely responsible for the audit opinion and cannot use direct assistance where prohibited by law/regulation."],[10038,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10039,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities relating to the work of an individual or organization in a field of expertise other than accounting or auditing, when used to obtain sufficient appropriate audit evidence."],[10039,"ISA 620.8–15","Using the Work of an Auditor's Expert","Evaluate competence, capabilities, and objectivity of the auditor's expert (including IESBA 2026 external expert ethics amendments), agree scope in writing, and evaluate adequacy of the expert's findings and assumptions; do not reference the expert in an unmodified report unless required by law."],[10039,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10040,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to form an opinion on the financial statements and the form and content of the auditor's report."],[10040,"ISA 700.20–49","Auditor's Report Structure & Unmodified Opinion","• Standardised report order (ISA 700.23–45): (1) Opinion (placed FIRST); (2) Basis for Opinion (including IESBA independence statement); (3) Going Concern (where applicable); (4) Key Audit Matters (ISA 701 for listed entities); (5) Other Information (ISA 720); (6) Responsibilities of Management & TCWG; (7) Auditor's Responsibilities (converged with China CSA 1501)."],[10040,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10041,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to communicate key audit matters (KAM) in the auditor's report for listed entities and where required."],[10041,"ISA 701.9–16","Key Audit Matters (KAM) Selection & Description","• Mandatory for audits of complete sets of general purpose financial statements of listed entities (ISA 701.5). • Selection funnel (ISA 701.9–10): matters communicated with TCWG → matters requiring significant auditor attention (high risk, significant judgements/estimates, significant events) → matters of MOST significance in the current period audit. • Description (ISA 701.13): explain WHY the matter was a KAM and HOW it was addressed in the audit (not a substitute for a modified opinion, converged with China CSA 1504)."],[10041,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10042,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibility to issue an appropriate report when a modification to the opinion (qualified, adverse, or disclaimer of opinion) is necessary."],[10042,"ISA 705.6–15","Modified Opinions Matrix (Material vs. Pervasive)","• Financial statements are materially misstated: Material but NOT pervasive → Qualified Opinion (保留意见); Material AND pervasive → Adverse Opinion (否定意见). • Inability to obtain sufficient appropriate audit evidence (scope limitation): Material but NOT pervasive → Qualified Opinion; Material AND pervasive → Disclaimer of Opinion (无法表示意见) (converged with China CSA 1502)."],[10042,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10043,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with additional communication in the auditor's report when the auditor considers it necessary to draw users' attention to a matter via an Emphasis of Matter or Other Matter paragraph."],[10043,"ISA 706.8–12","Emphasis of Matter & Other Matter Paragraphs","Emphasis of Matter (EoM) highlights a matter appropriately presented/disclosed in the FS that is fundamental to users' understanding (without modifying the opinion); Other Matter (OM) communicates a matter relevant to understanding the audit/auditor's responsibilities. Neither replaces KAM (ISA 701) or Going Concern (ISA 570)."],[10043,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10044,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities relating to comparative information in an audit of financial statements."],[10044,"ISA 710.7–19","Comparative Information (Corresponding Figures vs. Comparative FS)","Under Corresponding Figures, opinion refers only to current period (unless prior period was modified/misstated/unaudited); under Comparative Financial Statements, opinion refers to each period presented."],[10044,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10045,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities relating to other information, whether financial or non-financial information, included in an entity's annual report."],[10045,"ISA 720.13–24","Auditor's Responsibilities Relating to Other Information","Read and consider all other information in the annual report (MD&A, chairman's statement) for material inconsistency with the FS or auditor's knowledge; include a dedicated 'Other Information' section in the auditor's report (ISA 720.21)."],[10045,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (ISQM 1–2, ISA 200–720) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10046,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with special considerations in the application of ISAs to an audit of financial statements prepared in accordance with a special purpose framework."],[10046,"ISA 800.8–14","Special Purpose Framework Audits","Determine acceptability of special purpose framework (tax, cash-receipts, regulatory, contractual) and include an Emphasis of Matter paragraph alerting users that the FS are prepared under a special purpose framework and may not be suitable for another purpose (ISA 800.14)."],[10046,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10047,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with special considerations in the application of ISAs to an audit of a single financial statement or of a specific element, account, or item of a financial statement."],[10047,"ISA 805.7–17","Single Financial Statement or Specific Element Audits","Apply all relevant ISAs adapted to the single statement/element; evaluate whether auditing an isolated element without auditing the complete FS is practicable and consider interrelated items."],[10047,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10048,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the auditor's responsibilities relating to an engagement to report on summary financial statements derived from financial statements audited in accordance with ISAs."],[10048,"ISA 810.6–26","Engagements to Report on Summary Financial Statements","Accept engagement ONLY when also engaged to audit the complete FS from which summary FS are derived (ISA 810.5); opine on whether summary FS are consistent in all material respects with, or a fair summary of, the audited FS."],[10048,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10049,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Standalone global auditing standard designed specifically for audits of financial statements of less complex entities (LCEs), providing a proportionate risk-based audit framework effective for periods beginning on or after 15 Dec 2025."],[10049,"ISA for LCE Parts 1–10","Proportionate Standalone Audit Standard for Less Complex Entities","Effective for periods beginning on or after 15 Dec 2025; prohibits use for listed entities, public interest entities (PIEs), or complex groups; delivers the same 'reasonable assurance' level as full ISAs through streamlined, self-contained risk-based requirements."],[10049,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 3 (ISA for LCE) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10050,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the practitioner's responsibilities when engaged to perform a review of historical financial statements when the practitioner is not the auditor of the entity's financial statements."],[10050,"ISRE 2400.43–92","Limited Assurance Review of Historical Financial Statements","Practitioner performs primarily inquiry and analytical procedures to obtain limited assurance and express a negative-assurance conclusion ('nothing has come to our attention that causes us to believe...')."],[10050,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10051,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Establishes standards and provides guidance on the auditor's professional responsibilities when undertaking an engagement to review interim financial information of an audit client."],[10051,"ISRE 2410.12–43","Interim Financial Information Review by the Entity's Auditor","Leverages the auditor's existing understanding of the entity and internal control to perform targeted inquiries and analytical procedures on interim statements (e.g., IAS 34 condensed interims), issuing a limited-assurance review conclusion."],[10051,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10052,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Umbrella standard for reasonable and limited assurance engagements other than audits or reviews of historical financial information."],[10052,"ISAE 3000.24–69","Assurance Engagements Other than Audits/Reviews","Establishes preconditions (suitable criteria, appropriate underlying subject matter, rational purpose), distinguishes reasonable vs. limited assurance work effort, and specifies assurance report elements."],[10052,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10053,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Establishes standards and provides guidance on engagements to examine and report on prospective financial information (forecasts and projections)."],[10053,"ISAE 3400.8–27","Examination of Prospective Financial Information","Obtain sufficient appropriate evidence whether management's best-estimate assumptions are not unreasonable (forecasts) or hypothetical assumptions are consistent with purpose (projections), and express negative assurance on assumptions plus positive assurance on proper preparation."],[10053,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10054,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with assurance engagements undertaken by a professional accountant in public practice to provide a report for use by user entities and their auditors on the controls at a service organization (Type 1 & Type 2)."],[10054,"ISAE 3402.13–53","Service Organization Controls Reports (Type 1 & Type 2)","Type 1 reports on fairness of system description and suitability of control design as of a point in time; Type 2 additionally tests and reports on operating effectiveness of controls over a specified period (used by user auditors under ISA 402)."],[10054,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10055,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with assurance engagements to report on an entity's greenhouse gas (GHG) statement, complementing ISAE 3000 (Revised) and ISSA 5000."],[10055,"ISAE 3410.17–76","Assurance on Greenhouse Gas (GHG) Statements","Covers organizational/operational boundaries, quantification methods, emission factors, Scope 1–3 uncertainty, and site-level verification for standalone GHG statements (complementing ISSA 5000)."],[10055,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10056,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with reasonable assurance engagements undertaken by a practitioner to report on the responsible party's compilation of pro forma financial information included in a prospectus."],[10056,"ISAE 3420.13–35","Assurance on Pro Forma Financial Information in a Prospectus","Reasonable assurance engagement testing whether pro forma financial information has been properly compiled on the basis of applicable criteria (e.g., acquisition adjustments) — does not re-audit the underlying historical FS."],[10056,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10057,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Overarching global standard for limited and reasonable sustainability assurance engagements across all sustainability reporting frameworks (including IFRS S1/S2), effective for periods beginning on or after 15 Dec 2026."],[10057,"ISSA 5000 (Eff. Dec 2026)","Sustainability Assurance: Limited vs. Reasonable & Value Chain","• Profession-agnostic, framework-neutral global standard for sustainability assurance engagements (applicable to IFRS S1/S2, ESRS, GRI, etc.) effective for periods beginning on or after 15 Dec 2026. • Covers both Limited Assurance (primarily inquiry and analytical procedures) and Reasonable Assurance (tests of controls and substantive procedures), addressing double vs. financial materiality, forward-looking estimates, value chain data, and fraud/greenwashing risks. • Preconditions: requires firm quality management at least as demanding as ISQM 1 and ethical/independence requirements at least as demanding as IESBA Part 5 (IESSA) (converged with China Sustainability Assurance Standard No. 6101)."],[10057,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: upcoming. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 4 (ISSA 5000) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10058,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the practitioner's responsibilities when engaged to perform an agreed-upon procedures (AUP) engagement and the form and content of the AUP report."],[10058,"ISRS 4400.19–32","Agreed-Upon Procedures (AUP) Engagements","Practitioner performs specific procedures agreed with engaging party and reports ONLY factual findings — NO assurance or opinion is expressed; independence is not mandatory unless required by law/engagement terms (must disclose whether independent)."],[10058,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10059,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Deals with the practitioner's responsibilities when engaged to assist management with the preparation and presentation of historical financial information without obtaining any assurance on that information."],[10059,"ISRS 4410.24–41","Compilation Engagements","Applies accounting/financial reporting expertise to assist management in preparing and presenting historical financial information; NO assurance is obtained or expressed, and the compilation report explicitly states neither an audit nor a review was performed."],[10059,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IAASB 2026 Handbook): https://www.iaasb.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-quality-management-auditing-review-sustainability-and-other-assurance Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (ISA 800–810, ISRE, ISAE, ISRS & Assurance Framework) Local Private Full-Text Import: Place the free official 2026 IAASB Handbook PDF in local_pdfs/ and run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py`."],[10060,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Establishes the five fundamental principles (integrity, objectivity, professional competence and due care, confidentiality, professional behavior) and the conceptual framework for all professional accountants in business (Part 2) and public practice (Part 3), incorporating 2026 external expert and sustainability reporting revisions."],[10060,"IESBA Sec 110–390","Five Fundamental Principles, Threats & 2026 External Expert Rules","• Five Fundamental Principles (Section 110): Integrity, Objectivity, Professional Competence and Due Care, Confidentiality, and Professional Behavior. • Five Threat Categories (Section 120): Self-interest, Self-review, Advocacy, Familiarity, and Intimidation — addressed by eliminating circumstances, applying safeguards, or declining/ending the engagement. • NOCLAR (Sections 260 & 360): structured response framework for Non-Compliance with Laws and Regulations. • 2026 Handbook Additions (effective 15 Dec 2026): new Section 290 (PAIBs) and Section 390 (PAPPs) governing ethical evaluation when using the work of an external expert, plus sustainability reporting ethics revisions."],[10060,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IESBA 2026 Handbook): https://www.ethicsboard.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-code-ethics-professional-accountants Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (Parts 1–3, Part 4A & Part 4B) Official Free PDF (Vol. 1): https://ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2026-09/2026-IESBA-HB-Volume-1.pdf Local Private Full-Text Import: Run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py --download-iesba` (or place the PDF in local_pdfs/)."],[10061,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Sets out the International Independence Standards applicable to audit and review engagements, including public interest entity (PIE) definitions, fee-related provisions, non-assurance services restrictions, and partner rotation."],[10061,"IESBA Sec 400–600","Audit & Review Independence: PIEs, Fees, NAS & Partner Rotation","• Independence of Mind and Independence in Appearance required throughout the engagement period and period covered by the financial statements (Section 400). • Public Interest Entities — PIEs (Section 400.17): expanded definition covering publicly traded entities, banks, insurers, and entities holding assets in a fiduciary capacity. • Fee-related provisions (Section 410): public fee transparency for PIEs and fee-dependency thresholds (>15% for 2 consecutive years triggers mandatory pre-issuance EQR; >15% for 5 consecutive years triggers resignation for PIEs). • Non-Assurance Services — NAS (Section 600): prohibits creating a self-review threat for PIE audit clients (no materiality qualifier) and requires TCWG concurrence; Key Audit Partner rotation limited to 7 years on / 5 years cooling-off for PIE engagement partners (Section 540)."],[10061,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IESBA 2026 Handbook): https://www.ethicsboard.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-code-ethics-professional-accountants Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (Parts 1–3, Part 4A & Part 4B) Official Free PDF (Vol. 1): https://ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2026-09/2026-IESBA-HB-Volume-1.pdf Local Private Full-Text Import: Run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py --download-iesba` (or place the PDF in local_pdfs/)."],[10062,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Sets out independence standards for assurance engagements other than audit, review, and sustainability assurance engagements covered by Part 5."],[10062,"IESBA Sec 900–990","Independence for Other Assurance Engagements","• Applies to assurance engagements other than audits/reviews of historical financial statements (Part 4A) and sustainability assurance engagements (Part 5 — IESSA). • Covers financial interests, loans/guarantees, business/family relationships, long association, and provision of non-assurance services to assurance clients (ISAE 3000 / 3402 / 3410)."],[10062,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IESBA 2026 Handbook): https://www.ethicsboard.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-code-ethics-professional-accountants Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 1 (Parts 1–3, Part 4A & Part 4B) Official Free PDF (Vol. 1): https://ifacweb.blob.core.windows.net/publicfiles/2026-09/2026-IESBA-HB-Volume-1.pdf Local Private Full-Text Import: Run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py --download-iesba` (or place the PDF in local_pdfs/)."],[10063,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Profession-agnostic ethics and independence standards for all sustainability assurance practitioners (Volume 2 of the 2026 IESBA Handbook), effective for sustainability assurance engagements for periods beginning on or after 15 Dec 2026."],[10063,"IESBA Part 5 (Eff. Dec 2026)","Sustainability Assurance Ethics & Value-Chain Independence","• Volume 2 of the 2026 IESBA Handbook (effective 15 Dec 2026): applies equally to BOTH professional accountants and non-accountant sustainability assurance practitioners. • Establishes independence standards equivalent in rigor to Part 4A for sustainability assurance engagements of PIEs, plus tailored independence rules for value-chain entities and using the work of another practitioner or external expert."],[10063,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (IESBA 2026 Handbook (Volume 2)): https://www.ethicsboard.org/publications/2026-handbook-international-code-ethics-professional-accountants Status: upcoming. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally. 2026 Handbook Volume: Volume 2 (Part 5 — IESSA) Local Private Full-Text Import: Run `python3 scripts/import_private_intl_pdfs.py --download-iesba` (or place the PDF in local_pdfs/)."]]);
